pt in the\nprefix, so a message that adds a tool group re-creates the cache once. The default set covers most\nmessages, and the tool list is constant within a single tool loop.\n\n**Verify:** I have not run this against the API. Send two messages within 5 minutes. The second should show\n`cache_read_input_tokens` covering the whole prompt. Then trigger `save_fact` and send a third message.\n`cache_read` should still cover the instructions, and `cache_creation` should be only about the size of the tail.\nCaveat: the model has a minimum cacheable prefix, which is 1024 tokens on some models. The tools plus the\n~780-token instructions count toward it. If `cache_read` stays 0 for the static segment, the prefix is below\nthat minimum.\nE\npython3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('bot.py').read())\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3106,"cache_read_input_tokens":22876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3106},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36873090-a011-4418-bf10-c53f794b0155","uuid":"8a06edfe-3135-4997-ba72-c81ecc2f72fc","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:34:46.462Z","request_id":"req_011CgEN8DtgMaTkbUzWJsFNF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Hti6NqoYjDF92oPuu9Q4EN":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-nUwPP7 && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\nold=s[s.index(\"def build_system\"):s.index(\"# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\")]\nnew='''def build_system(a, today):\n    # Two cached segments: static instructions (byte-stable, no interpolation) and the\n    # volatile per-athlete tail. A save_fact only invalidates the tail.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_co